Risk-sensitive constraint: CVaR (Rockafellar–Uryasev form; Chow et al. 2018) For a cost $Z$ (large is bad) and $\alpha\in(0,1)$: $$ \operatorname{CVaR}_\alpha(Z)=\min_{
u\in\mathbb R}\Big\{
u+ rac{1}{1-\alpha}\,\mathbb E ig[(Z-
u)^+ ig]\Big\} $$ the average of the worst $(1-\alpha)$-fraction of outcomes: $\alpha	o1$ is the tail, $\alpha	o0$ recovers $\mathbb E[Z]$. A risk constraint reads $\operatorname{CVaR}_\alpha(\sum_t c_t)\le d$.

Uniform error bound for GP sample paths (Lederer et al. 2019, Thm. 3.1) $f$ is a sample from $\mathcal{GP}(0,k)$ on a compact $X$; observations $y=f(x)+\epsilon$ with i.i.d. $\mathcal N(0,\sigma_n^2)$ noise; $k$ continuous with Lipschitz constant $L_k$; $f$ Lipschitz with constant $L_f$; $M(	au,X)$ the $	au$-covering number of $X$. The posterior mean $
u_N$ and standard deviation $\sigma_N$ are continuous, with Lipschitz constant $L_{
u_N}$ and modulus of continuity $\omega_{\sigma_N}$ bounded by $$ L_{
u_N}\le L_k\sqrt N\,\|(K+\sigma_n^2I)^{-1}y\|,\qquad\omega_{\sigma_N}(	au)\le\sqrt{2	au L_k\Big(1+N\,\|(K+\sigma_n^2I)^{-1}\|\max_{x,x'\in X}k(x,x')\Big)} $$ For any $\delta\in(0,1)$ and $	au\gt0$, with $$  eta(	au)=2\log rac{M(	au,X)}{\delta},\qquad\gamma(	au)=(L_{
u_N}+L_f)	au+\sqrt{ eta(	au)}\,\omega_{\sigma_N}(	au) $$ $$ \Pr\Big[\,|f(x)-
u_N(x)|\le\sqrt{ eta(	au)}\,\sigma_N(x)+\gamma(	au)\ \  orall x\in X\Big]\ge1-\delta,\qquad M(	au,[0,r]^d)\le ig(1+r\sqrt d/	au ig)^d $$ The covering bound uses the diameter $r\sqrt d$ of the cube, as in the paper’s appendix; its main-text eq. (9) prints $(1+r/	au)^d$ with $r$ the edge length, which in the Euclidean metric is too small in high dimension.

Assumptions: what SafeOpt needs (1) Safe seed: a non-empty $S_0 \subseteq D$ with $f(x) \ge h$ for all $x \in S_0$. (2) RKHS regularity: $\|f\|_k \le B$ for a known kernel $k$ (module convention; Sui et al. write $\|f\|_k^2 \le B$). (3) Lipschitz continuity: $|f(x) - f(x')| \le L\,d(x,x')$ for a known metric $d$ on $D$ and a known constant $L$. (4) Noise $n_t$ zero-mean given the history and uniformly bounded by $\sigma$ (Sui et al.); later papers assume $\sigma$-sub-Gaussian noise, $\mathbb{E}[e^{
u n_t} \mid 	ext{history}] \le e^{
u^2\sigma^2/2}$ for all $
u \in \mathbb R$.

CVaR, Rockafellar–Uryasev form (as used by Chow et al. 2018, Eq. 1) $$ \mathrm{CVaR}_\alpha(Z)=\min_{
u\in\mathbb R}\Big\{
u+ rac{1}{1-\alpha}\,\mathbb E ig[(Z-
u)_+ ig]\Big\},\qquad \alpha\in(0,1) $$ the minimiser being $
u^\star=\mathrm{VaR}_\alpha(Z)$. For a continuous distribution $\mathrm{CVaR}_\alpha(Z)=\mathbb E[Z\mid Z\ge\mathrm{VaR}_\alpha(Z)]$: the mean of the worst $(1-\alpha)$ fraction of outcomes; $\alpha	o1$ is the extreme tail, $\alpha	o0$ recovers the mean.
